theory.intro:
A **line of best fit** is a single straight line, drawn by eye, that follows the overall trend of a scatter plot. When a computer calculates it exactly it is called a **regression line**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (6.2,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (0,4.4);
\node at (6.6,0) {$x$};
\node at (0,4.8) {$y$};
\foreach \p in {(0.8,1.3),(1.4,1.1),(2.0,1.9),(2.6,1.8),(3.2,2.6),(3.8,2.4),(4.4,3.3),(4.8,3.0)} {\fill \p circle (2.4pt);}
\draw[thick] (0.8,1.04) -- (4.8,3.24);
\node[right] at (0.3,3.9) {line of best fit};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

